 "notes": "All commands follow repo/reproduce_scripts/reproduce_slab.py, with the 'train' and 'evaluate' base commands plus the per-method arguments as written. `--n_runs 10` is the script's total_seed. No values were taken from the paper.\n\ndata_steps is empty. The slab data is generated in memory by data/slab_loader.py and utils/slab_data.py at every train and test run, and no data-preparation script exists.\n\nSource 1 and Source 2 come from the eval step (test.py --test_metric per_domain_acc --acc_data_case train). It prints both source-domain accuracies on one line per run (evaluation/per_domain_acc.py:79), so there are two parsers, one per domain index (0 and 1). Runs are split on the 'Data Case: train' line that data/slab_loader.py:54 prints once per run. test.py prints no run header of its own.\n\nTarget comes from the train log. Each epoch prints 'Current Best Epoch: k with Test Accuracy: v' (erm_match.py:160, mmd.py:172, dann.py:149). The last such line in a run block is the target-domain accuracy at the best source-validation epoch. This is the same quantity as the 'Final Test Accuracy (Source Validation)' summary line, which is printed over all runs, so I parse the per-run line instead. Runs are split on 'Run N' (train.py:207).\n\ntrain.py and test.py use `--dataset`, which argparse accepts as an abbreviation of `--dataset_name`. The scripts' --help fails at this commit (unescaped %), but the shipped commands are used unchanged.\n\nRow-name mapping: CDANN is script method 'c-dann', and CORAL / C-CORAL use method_name mmd with `--gaussian 0`. PerfMatch is match_case 1.0 and RandMatch is match_case 0.0."
